From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:21:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 306/306] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Train the signal
 settings of each byte

The MRC of the Lenovo firmware trains, byte by byte, the settings that
shape the signal (its power training: TrainDDROptParam for the write
drive strength, the transmit equalisation, the read termination and the
receiver bias), where the NRI sets the same for every byte. On a
ThinkPad W541 it leaves the read termination of bytes 5 to 7 of channel
1, the narrowest of the board with the NRI, 3 to 7 codes stronger than
that of the other bytes, and a transmit equalisation of 51 to 56.

Add HASWELL_NRI_OPT_PARAMS: after the 1D centring, for the write drive
strength and equalisation, then the read termination and bias, set
every byte to each value of a list in turn, measure the margins that
the setting acts on with the margin library (the tests and loop counts
of the MRC, all the ranks at once), and keep for each byte the value
with the widest eye, if it beats the one it had by three steps. Power
is not weighed. The writes and the reads are centred again after their
settings, and optimise_comp() moves the mean of the offsets into the
global compensation codes, as it was written to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ieb14139e415270f599e36c98945d0ab931f804fb
